{"manifest_version":1,"engine_version":"0.2.0-alpha.1","plan_spec_version":1,"stages":[{"name":"assert","input_kind":"checks.jsonl","output_kind":"checks.jsonl","args_schema":{"$ref":"#/definitions/AssertArgs","definitions":{"AssertArgs":{"description":"Args for [`Assert`]: a scalar predicate `actual <op> expected` (± tolerance).","properties":{"actual":{"description":"The measured value (typically threaded in from an upstream metric).","format":"double","type":"number"},"expected":{"description":"The bound to compare against.","format":"double","type":"number"},"on_breach":{"$ref":"#/definitions/OnBreach","default":"block","description":"Breach policy (default: `block`)."},"op":{"$ref":"#/definitions/CmpOp","default":"ge","description":"The comparison operator."},"tolerance":{"default":0.0,"description":"Absolute tolerance applied to the comparison (default 0). Band semantics: `Ge`/`Gt` relax the bound to `expected - tolerance`; `Le`/`Lt` relax it to `expected + tolerance`; `Eq`/`Ne` treat `|actual - expected| <= tolerance` as equal. Note a `NaN` `actual` fails every predicate except `Ne` (NaN is unequal to everything) — intentional: an unmeasured value never satisfies a data-quality floor.","format":"double","type":"number"}},"required":["actual","expected"],"type":"object"},"CmpOp":{"description":"Comparison operator for [`Assert`].","enum":["ge","gt","le","lt","eq","ne"],"type":"string"},"OnBreach":{"description":"How a check treats a breach. `Block` fails the node (fail-closed — the executor skips every downstream); `Warn` records a lineage breach event and passes through so the DAG continues.","enum":["block","warn"],"type":"string"}}}},{"name":"check_jsonl","input_kind":"checks.jsonl","output_kind":"checks.jsonl","args_schema":{"$ref":"#/definitions/CheckJsonlArgs","definitions":{"CheckJsonlArgs":{"description":"Args for [`CheckJsonl`]: row-count bounds + breach policy.","properties":{"max_rows":{"default":null,"description":"Maximum row count (inclusive). `N